      "side": 1,
      "message": "Thank you, that example demonstrates the problem perfectly.\n\nOne interesting thing to note is that if you make the lambda explicitly `consteval`, the compiler gives a slightly different error message: `call to immediate function ...` becomes `call to consteval function ...`. If you look up `immediate` on https://en.cppreference.com/cpp/language/lambda, you\u0027ll see that adding `consteval` to a lambda makes it an immediate function. There\u0027s also a bunch more on immediate functions on https://en.cppreference.com/cpp/language/consteval. I guess Clang is distinguishing between the lambda being implicitly immediate vs explicitly (consteval).\n\nAnyway, I think you\u0027re making the right call with using `constexpr` only in the next change, and forcing us to pass in unsigned values.",
